course: dictionary
lesson: 1712
title: Cipher: a secret code and more
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A cipher is a secret code. The letters of a message are swapped or mixed up by a rule, so only people who know the rule can read it. In a Caesar cipher, every letter moves a fixed number of places along the alphabet. With a shift of 3, A becomes D and B becomes E.
explain: A cipher can also mean the coded message itself. In a story, the heroes often have to crack a cipher, which means working out the secret rule and reading the hidden message. Phrases like «break a cipher» and «a cipher key» use the same idea.
explain: Cipher has two more meanings. A person with no power who just does what others say can be called a cipher, as in «The king was a mere cipher». The old word for the figure zero, 0, is also cipher. Context tells you which meaning is right: look at the words around it.
fact: Cipher means a secret code in which letters are swapped or mixed up by a rule.
fact: «The idea of zero came from India; Arab mathematicians passed it to Europe, and its name came from Arabic "ṣifr", empty, which also gave "cipher".»
fact: A Caesar cipher moves every letter a fixed number of places along the alphabet: A becomes D with a shift of 3.
fact: In the Second World War, code-breakers at Bletchley Park, including Alan Turing, worked to break the German Enigma cipher.
fact: A person who has no power and just does what others say can also be called a cipher.
exercise: «The message was written in cipher, so nobody in the class could read it.» What does cipher mean here? | A type of sum with no answer | * A secret code | A loud shout | A kind of cup
exercise: Which word means a person with no power who just does what others say? | Scholar | * Cipher | Champion | Monarch
exercise: In a Caesar cipher, A becomes D. How far does each letter move? | It does not move at all | One place back | Ten places along the alphabet | * Three places along the alphabet
test: In a Caesar cipher with a shift of 3, what letter does B become? | A | C | F | * E
test: In the story, the heroes must crack the cipher. What does crack mean here? | Write the message again in big letters | Forget the message | Break the paper it is written on | * Work out the secret rule and read the hidden message
exam: Which Arabic word, meaning empty, gave us the word cipher? | Bletchley | * ṣifr | Caesar | Enigma
